// Analyzed file list for wb2axip_axi3_reorder. Paths are relative to the
// PACKAGE ROOT: the elaboration recipe is sourced with the package root as cwd
// and `slang` is run from there too, so one spelling serves both.
//
// The round appends one `../submission/<worker>.sv` line per worker to the end
// of this file (v5/round.py), which resolves to <run_root>/submission from the
// same cwd. Do not add a trailing `-y`/library directive after the file list --
// an appended source line has to stay a source line.
//
// ONE analyzed file. The two wb2axip RTL files are NOT listed: `ft/tb.sv`
// pulls them in with `include at file scope, exactly as the upstream task's
// `tcl/setup.tcl` does, and listing them as well would declare both modules
// twice. `+incdir+rtl` is what makes those includes resolve.
//
// `ft/tb.sv` also `undefs FORMAL before the includes, which is what keeps the
// two files' own ZipCPU formal harnesses out of the elaboration. That is the
// task's statement of its environment, and it lives in the source, not here.

// --- one Slang-only switch, and why it is here rather than in the source ----
// `axi3reorder.v:337` reads `sr_valid[gk+1]` where `sr_valid` is
// `reg [NSREG-1:0]`, inside `else if (sr_advance[gk] && gk<NSREG-1)`. At
// gk = NSREG-1 the index is one past the end and the branch is statically
// dead, so nothing ever reads it -- and an out-of-range bit-select of a packed
// vector is legal Verilog anyway (IEEE 1800 11.5.1: the value is x). Jasper
// takes it. Slang promotes `index-oob` to an ERROR and will not elaborate the
// package without this line, which fails the `v6_dataset/elab_local.py` gate.
//
// It lives here because this list is the only channel to Slang:
// `taskdefs.slang_args` copies every non-comment line into
// `lists/tc_elab.files.slang` and passes that with `-f`. Jasper's `analyze -f`
// does not understand `-W`, so `lists/tc_elab.tcl` reads this list itself and
// drops any line starting with `-` before calling `analyze`. That is one place
// deciding it, and it is documented at both ends.
//
// The alternative was editing the DUT. It was rejected: the target is a
// property ABOUT `axi3reorder`, and a package whose design source is not the
// upstream source is a different experiment.
-Wno-index-oob

+incdir+rtl

// --- the AXI3 reorder DUT, the reference queues, the target and the covers --
ft/tb.sv

// --- phase-1 candidate targets, LAST: a `bind` must be analyzed after the
// --- module it binds into.  A PLAIN path line, not a `-` switch: this
// --- package's `tc_elab.tcl` reads this list itself and drops `-`-prefixed
// --- lines before calling `analyze`, so only plain paths reach Jasper.
sva/targets_wb2axip_axi3_reorder.sv
